/-!
Kernel-checked foundations for both theorem families over pure S.

For Result B,
`PureSFormal.Research.ProtectedTrieCertificateEnumeration` is the public
entry point.  It quantifies over an explicit finite ordered-binary source
instance and exports persistent certificate enumeration,
all-reduct permanence, exact finite range, cofinal recovery, an embedded
computation-history tree, and an address-complete adjacent-step canonical
path.  Its total current-term observer parses protected literal records and
checks their decoded tableaux with the encoded source transition relation.

`PureSFormal.Research.ProtectedPrefixGeneratorCalibration` isolates the
generic permanence theorem and records exact-range and cofinality as separate
generator capabilities.

For Result A, `PureSFormal.WeakPathUniversality` is the separate public
selected-path theorem and uses its persistent-cursor scheduler.  Result B
uses the unrestricted pure-`S` reduction cone and its checked observer.
-/
